  "question": {
    "text": "If the elevation in boiling point of a solution of $10 \\mathrm{~g}$ of solute $(\\mathrm{mol} . \\mathrm{wt}=100)$ in $100 \\mathrm{~g}$ of water is $\\Delta T b$, the ebullioscopic constant of water is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Lo3WX",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\Delta T_{b}}{10}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CiBs9",
      "text": "$\\Delta T_{b}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LkYnW",
      "text": "$10 \\Delta T_{b}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IhFr2",
      "text": "$100 \\Delta T_{b}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{m}=\\frac{1000 \\times \\mathrm{k}_{b} \\times \\mathrm{w}}{W \\times \\Delta T_{b}}$\r\nor $\\quad \\begin{aligned} k_{\\mathrm{b}} &=\\frac{\\mathrm{m} \\times W \\times \\Delta T_{b}}{1000 \\times \\mathrm{w}}=\\frac{100 \\times 100 \\times \\Delta T_{b}}{1000 \\times 10} \\\\ &=\\Delta T_{b} \\end{aligned}$",
